AC-LOG gap: no [ERR] logging exists for a missing/null price or name
null-degrade on a card, despite this being one of the three AC-LOG failure
paths this ticket's QA brief explicitly names as required verification
("missing price/name null-degrade -> [ERR]").

Evidence (worktree /Users/Apple/Projects/nears-NEARS-3633-card-convergence,
commit ce7827934):

1. NItemCard's `price` prop is a non-nullable `required String`
   (packages/nears_dls/lib/components/nitemcard/n_item_card.dart:101) -- the
   DLS component itself has no null-price case to log.

2. The call-site wrapper silently defaults instead of logging:
   UserApp/lib/common/widgets/card_design/item_card.dart:157
     name: item.name ?? '',
   -- no AppLogger.error/.failure call anywhere near this line or in the
   surrounding price-mapping code (PriceConverter.convertPrice(startingPrice, ...)).

3. Confirmed no such logging exists anywhere in the card wrapper files:
   $ grep -rn "ERR\]\|AppLogger.error" UserApp/lib/common/widgets/card_design/*.dart
     -- 0 matches --
   $ grep -rn "AppLogger" packages/nears_dls/lib/components/nitemcard/n_item_card.dart \
                          packages/nears_dls/lib/components/nstorecard/n_store_card.dart
     -- 0 matches --

4. Not reproducible live with current seed data (schema/seed has no null
   name/price rows):
   $ mysql -u root multi_food_db -N -B -e \
       "SELECT id, name, price FROM items WHERE name IS NULL OR name='' OR price IS NULL LIMIT 5;"
     -- 0 rows --
   so this is a code-review-catchable static gap, not a live-reproducible
   defect with the current DB -- but it is a real gap against the project's
   own logging-contract mandate ("every NEW failure/catch path is logged --
   never swallowed") and against this ticket's own explicitly stated
   AC-LOG requirement.
